  "$comment": "Brand name -> the US-listed company whose SEC filings company_financials (S13, PLAN §5.2) reads. Names and tickers only, no figures (D29). A brand matches only when the entity resolves exactly (D20) to one of these names; any other brand gets UNAVAILABLE with NOT_A_LISTED_COMPANY, never a guess. `note` says when the brand is part of a larger company: SEC figures are company-wide, never brand-level. `relation` says how the brand relates to the company (Part 9 open issue 6): `self` when the company is named for the brand and it is the main business (Nike, Starbucks, Marriott Hotels), so its figures are shown with the note; `parent` when the brand is one of several inside a larger company (Sprite, HOKA, Marriott Bonvoy), whose filings never break it out: the agent then shows no figures and says so (NOT_SEPARATELY_REPORTED, naming `parent_name`). Every entry states its relation. Every ticker was checked against the SEC ticker map and has us-gaap revenue in its company facts; foreign IFRS filers are left out. The match is on the name Qloo returns (case aside), so each brand is listed under that name as well as its common one; check every key against Qloo with `pnpm exec tsx tools/dev/listed-brands.ts` after editing this file. Re-check when a company is acquired, taken private or renames its ticker.",
